WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.200
-It's a pleasure to have you
on the show. I'm a big fan.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.501
Congrats on --
You've been knocking it

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.234
out of the park
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:10.067
-Oh, your words, you know.
-It is, but, yeah.

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:11.834
But you've actually
been crushing it.

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:14.200
-Thanks, man.
-I remember when you first

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.634
got cast, and Higgins
and Lorne were like,

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:19.200
"You've got to see this kid.
He's unbelievable."

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.934
I was like, "Oh, I can't wait."
'Cause I love impressions.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:26.400
The first -- The first scene
anyone ever saw of you,

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.033
you're in the cold open.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:32.100
-I'm in the cold open
of my first episode of the show,

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.834
and I just walked out
in full Biden makeup.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.033
-Yeah.

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:37.901
-Which I think I knew
for about --

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:40.100
I had known at that point
for about 24 hours

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.934
that I was going to do that.

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:44.501
And it was very surreal.
-When I was on the show

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:47.267
and just starting out,
I was not in all of the shows.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:48.701
I was barely in --

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:50.367
I would call my mom like, "I
didn't make it into the show.

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:52.167
Don't watch.
Or -- Don't get excited.

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.667
I'm in the opening credits,
but then I'm not in show."

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:59.701
-I fully was like, "Mom, Dad.
Just hang out, watch me.

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.901
I'm going to wait in the wings.
I'm going to learn the ropes."

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:03.267
-Yeah.
-And then, like, Friday night,

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:05.133
they're like, "We're putting you
in full Biden makeup.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.100
You need to riff
in front of the camera

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.834
so we can make sure
that we can do this.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.100
By the way, you are doing it
and you have to go out now.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.267
It's actually Saturday
at midnight right now.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:14.567
You have to go right now."

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:17.467
I had no time to think about it.
I just jumped in.

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:20.567
And I was like, "Alright.
Let's find this guy.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.267
Let's find the voice."

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.167
-Yeah. How do you find Biden?
Did you have him?

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.634
-Well, you know, he's a mixture
of a few different impressions.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.534
I did have an Owen Wilson.

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:30.734
And Biden has this, like --

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.634
You know in Owen Wilson movies

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.567
he's always giving, like,
a pump-up speech

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:36.534
halfway through
to another character?

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:40.467
Like -- [as Owen Wilson] "I saw
you up there. You're so great!

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:43.534
I thought, wow, I could do that!
We're gonna do that.

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:44.834
We're gonna get
everybody together.

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.767
We're gonna move forward.
Good jobs."

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:47.968
-Wow.

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:49.400
-[Normal voice]
So he has that pump-up guy.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.767
-Yeah.

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.934
-And then he does like --
And then he's got

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:54.667
Nicolas Cage vibes sometimes.

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:56.801
Like, he's really proud
of himself.

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:59.067
You know, Nicolas Cage
has that kind of voice like...

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.300
[As Cage] "You know, I am proud
of Build Back Better.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:04.968
I...just want to
make signature policies.

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:08.567
And it's -- it's -- this is
gonna be good for everybody.

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:10.634
If you don't like it,
that's too tough."

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:11.901
-Wow.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:13.968
-"We got to protect
our Bill of Rights.

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:15.834
We're gonna steal
the Bill of Rights."

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:17.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.834
[Normal voice] And then
you finish it off with that --

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:22.734
that irascible Biden
who's like --

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:25.467
You know, a voter is like,
"You're taking my guns away."

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:26.868
And he's like,
"Oh, n-nobody said

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:28.934
I was taking your guns away!

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:31.367
No one's gonna ever --
I never said that.

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:32.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:35.267
I never said
I was gonna do that."

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:36.901
Then you just mix it all
together.

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:39.033
[As Biden] "It's not about
yesterday. It's about today.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.534
Moving forward, bring people
together, good union jobs.

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:43.667
Emissions. Lower emissions.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:46.467
We're gonna be competitive,
competitive with everybody."

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:48.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.701
-Wow.
-[Normal voice] That's Biden.

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:52.267
That's fantastic, buddy.

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:54.834
-He's just three guys, you know?
-That's fantastic.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:56.267
I know that you're --

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:58.667
Was it always your goal
to be on "Saturday Night Live"?

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:00.434
-I always wanted to do it.

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:04.834
I would stay up late, sort of
sneak some viewings of it,

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:06.601
even though we had church
in the morning.

00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:09.901
I'd be like, "Yeah, I'm old
enough to watch this content."

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:12.334
-You brought me something that
you have hanging in your office.

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:14.701
-Okay. Yeah. So my brother
came and visited "SNL."

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:16.367
I was too young
to come with him,

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:19.033
but he got an NBC page
to hand him a sheet of paper.

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:20.367
They didn't get into the show.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.000
They were in the stand-by line.
They didn't make it.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.834
So they just harassed
cast members on their way home.

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:28.067
And they got me this.

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:30.601
It's signed by Fred Armisen
and Bill Hader

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:32.701
and Jason Sudeikis.

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:35.534
And Fred here says,
"Hi, Austin. Keep writing."

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:37.667
My family calls me Austin.
-Wow.

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:39.667
-"Stay tough" from Bill Hader.

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:41.534
"Best of luck" from scribble,
scribble, scribble.

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:42.968
I think that's Sudeikis.

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:44.868
-Yeah. This is an NBC page --

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:47.434
I remember this --
actually this paper.

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:49.467
-Pre-smartphone.
-Telephone message. Yeah.

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.968
-And now this is hanging up
in my office,

00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:55.901
and I can just text
Fred Armisen whenever I --

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:59.501
I have a very specific "SNL,"
you know, quandary.

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.968
Like, "Is it normal to have
a texting marriage argument

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:05.200
while I'm in full
Lindsey Graham makeup?

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.767
Is this a normal feeling
to have?"

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:07.968
-The "SNL" questions you have.

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:11.801
I got to say, the first time
I think I saw you

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.601
was you did an impression
of Donald Trump,

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:16.801
which I think is the greatest
impression of Donald Trump.

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:18.734
-Oh, wow.
-It's such an interesting take,

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:20.400
and you did it
before anyone was doing this.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.467
-Aw, thank you.
-And I go, "What is going on?"

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:24.667
How did you figure out
you could do that?

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:27.000
-Well, let me just say
that I love that my fate

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.434
is bound to this man, you know?

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:31.534
I love --
Just any time he does something,

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:33.868
a relative will be like,
"What'd you think of that?"

00:04:33.868 --> 00:04:36.067
And I'd be like, "What a guy!"

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:37.634
-"I had nothing
to do with this guy.

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:39.567
I'm doing an impression
of this guy."

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:42.801
-Whew.
-A lot of people do it --

00:04:42.801 --> 00:04:45.767
[as Trump]
"They do the high voice --
You do the thing or whatever."

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:46.968
-There's, like, you know --

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:48.801
He's been around
for a long time,

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:50.701
so everybody
has their take on him.

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:53.734
But I -- My proudest moment

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:56.200
is that he called me out
in a speech.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.968
I don't know if it's a proud
moment to be mentioned

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:01.334
in a Trump rally,
but he was just like --

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.033
You know how he has that
stream-of-consciousness thing

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:05.701
where he bounces around
to a bunch of different
topics at once?

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:08.267
He was calling somebody
in Washington a liar.

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:11.067
Then he went -- [as Trump]
"He's a liar. The liar.

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:14.133
The liar.
Jon Lovitz. Jon Lovitz.

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:17.267
The show's not as good anymore.
It's not as good anymore.

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:19.567
We don't watch the show,
but they got a new guy doing me.

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:22.400
I hear he's pretty good.
I hear he's pretty good.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:27.968
They got a new guy doing me.
He's probably pretty good.

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:30.634
We don't know his name.
We don't watch the show."

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:32.901
-He's talking about someone
who's a liar, and he --

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:34.300
"The kid's pretty good."

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.601
-He loved the liar bit.
You know what I mean?

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:38.934
If he had just been like --
"Garth and Kat.

00:05:38.934 --> 00:05:41.267
We love Garth and Kat."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:43.033
"Remember Nick Burns?
We love Nick Burns."

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:45.734
-Oh, Nick Burns, yeah.
-"Nick Burns, he did computer,

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:47.767
and he was very good with iMac
and with computer."

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:50.200
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my goodness.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.968
It's unbelievable, buddy.

00:05:51.968 --> 00:05:55.367
-"SNL" fan Donald Trump.
-Now, I saw you.

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:58.100
We were in the halls,
getting our COVID test

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.400
the first time I saw you.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.234
And I go, "Hey, you're doing
great in the show, buddy.

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:02.634
Congratulations."

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:07.000
And we were talking quickly,
6 feet away, through masks,

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.868
and you were like --

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:11.200
I go, "You gotta come
on the show because I'm a fan."

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.334
You go, "I'd love to.
Maybe we can talk about Dylan."

00:06:13.334 --> 00:06:14.434
-Oh yeah.
-'Cause I know you're a fan

00:06:14.434 --> 00:06:15.534
of Bob Dylan.
-I know you're a fan

00:06:15.534 --> 00:06:17.801
of Bob Dylan.
I'm a fan of Bob Dylan.

00:06:17.801 --> 00:06:19.834
-I love Bob Dylan.
Did you get the new book?

00:06:19.834 --> 00:06:22.033
-I've got the new book,
"Philosophy of Modern Song."

00:06:22.033 --> 00:06:24.367
What you've really got to get
is the audio book.

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:26.901
'Cause if you ever listen
to him on Sirius XM,

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:29.367
he's like,
"Theme Time Radio on Sirius XM.

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:30.801
You're listening to Bob Dylan.

00:06:30.801 --> 00:06:34.634
Today's theme is flowers,
hydrangeas, chrysanthemums."

00:06:34.634 --> 00:06:37.167
And, like, the whole audio book
for his "Philosophy --"

00:06:37.167 --> 00:06:38.367
-I don't know
if I've ever heard anyone

00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:40.133
do a speaking impression
of Bob Dylan.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:45.501
-You should listen because his
voice is a little terrifying.

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:47.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:49.667
-Is there an era of Dylan
that you like doing the most?

00:06:49.667 --> 00:06:51.000
-There's too many to pick.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.400
I love the modern --

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.868
"Rough and Rowdy Ways,"
the last record, so good.

00:06:54.868 --> 00:06:56.400
So good.
-It was fantastic.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.968
-But the Bob Dylan that we love

00:06:57.968 --> 00:07:00.067
is the Greenwich Village
Bob Dylan.

00:07:00.067 --> 00:07:01.734
-Would you be up for showing us
your Bob Dylan impressions?

00:07:01.734 --> 00:07:02.968
-Yeah, I could walk
you through some.

00:07:02.968 --> 00:07:05.934
-Through the decades?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:09.801
-Yeah, sure.
If you insist.

00:07:09.801 --> 00:07:12.767
-With the holidays coming up,
maybe could we hear

00:07:12.767 --> 00:07:15.400
Bob Dylan singing
"Jingle Bells"?

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.267
-Oh, yeah, sure.
Yeah, we could

00:07:17.267 --> 00:07:19.968
maybe start it off with, like,
that folky

00:07:19.968 --> 00:07:21.400
Greenwich Village Bob Dylan.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.801
Here, let me get
this harmonica here.

00:07:23.801 --> 00:07:26.033
This will be helpful.

00:07:26.033 --> 00:07:28.968
[ As Bob Dylan]
♪ Jingle bells, jingle bells ♪

00:07:28.968 --> 00:07:31.434
♪ Jingle all the way ♪

00:07:31.434 --> 00:07:35.467
♪ Oh, what fun it is to ride ♪

00:07:35.467 --> 00:07:36.801
Heh-heh.

00:07:36.801 --> 00:07:38.534
[ Normal voice ] He's always
giggling on these songs.

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:40.367
[ As Dylan ] Heh-heh-heh.
♪ What fun it is to ride ♪

00:07:40.367 --> 00:07:42.000
Heh-heh.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.634
I think Calvin Coolidge
said that.

00:07:43.634 --> 00:07:46.200
[ Harmonica plays ]

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:51.701
It's like, "Some
professionalism, please, Bob."

00:07:51.701 --> 00:07:53.834
-But then he did --
how about the crooner,

00:07:53.834 --> 00:07:55.167
when he did a crooner,
kind of Sinatra --

00:07:55.167 --> 00:07:57.334
-The "Lay, Lady, Lay"...
-The National Skyline.

00:07:57.334 --> 00:07:59.534
-...National Skyline, Bob Dylan.

00:07:59.534 --> 00:08:01.667
He had a completely
different voice all of a sudden.

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:03.968
-Yes, he had...

00:08:03.968 --> 00:08:08.167
-It's like...
♪ Jingle bells, jingle bells ♪

00:08:08.167 --> 00:08:10.968
♪ Jingle all the way ♪

00:08:10.968 --> 00:08:15.300
♪ Oh, what fun it is
to r-i-i-ide ♪

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.834
♪ In a one-horse open sleigh ♪

00:08:17.834 --> 00:08:20.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:20.167 --> 00:08:22.400
Like, "Why are you
singing like that?

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.200
We don't even need you to sing.
You're Bob Dylan.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:25.567
-No, you already have
your own voice.

00:08:25.567 --> 00:08:27.000
But he created a new voice.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.767
But then he did the whole
rock-band tour,

00:08:29.767 --> 00:08:30.901
like, the Rolling Thunder.

00:08:30.901 --> 00:08:32.367
-And he's, like,
touring all over the world.

00:08:32.367 --> 00:08:33.601
He's filling arenas.

00:08:33.601 --> 00:08:35.367
He's got the
Rolling Thunder Revue band.

00:08:35.367 --> 00:08:38.000
That's my favorite Dylan
because he's unintelligible.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.334
He's just screaming.

00:08:39.334 --> 00:08:40.467
♪♪

00:08:40.467 --> 00:08:42.467
Yeah, here we go.

00:08:42.467 --> 00:08:45.400
♪♪

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.934
[ As Bob Dylan ]
♪ Oh, dashing through the snow ♪

00:08:48.934 --> 00:08:52.400
♪ Ooh, in a one-horse
open sleigh ♪

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:55.801
♪ Over the fields we go ♪

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:59.000
♪ Laughing,
laughing all the way ♪

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:02.534
♪ With your bells
on your bobtails ring ♪

00:09:02.534 --> 00:09:06.267
♪ And you're
making spirits bright ♪

00:09:06.267 --> 00:09:09.634
♪ What fun it is
to ride and sing ♪

00:09:09.634 --> 00:09:11.834
♪ On a sleighing song tonight ♪

00:09:11.834 --> 00:09:16.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:16.934 --> 00:09:19.133
[ Normal voice ]
I can hear you, Bob.

00:09:19.133 --> 00:09:20.267
I'm two towns over.

00:09:20.267 --> 00:09:21.467
I can hear you.
-He can hear you.

00:09:21.467 --> 00:09:23.300
You don't need
the microphone there.

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:26.234
How about '90s Dylan?

00:09:26.234 --> 00:09:28.334
-'90s Dylan,
he had a big comeback.

00:09:28.334 --> 00:09:29.567
"Time Out of Mind."

00:09:29.567 --> 00:09:31.033
He said,
"I'm never gonna sell out.

00:09:31.033 --> 00:09:32.634
I'll never do an ad."

00:09:32.634 --> 00:09:34.534
And then he did
a Victoria's Secret ad.

00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:35.734
[ Laughter ]

00:09:35.734 --> 00:09:38.667
And he's just singing
like a Disney vulture.

00:09:38.667 --> 00:09:40.167
[ Laughter ]

00:09:40.167 --> 00:09:43.667
He's singing like he crawled out
of a French crypt or something.

00:09:43.667 --> 00:09:46.501
And the songs have
this moody sexiness to them.

00:09:46.501 --> 00:09:50.367
[ Slow, creepy music plays ]

00:09:50.367 --> 00:09:52.234
[ As Bob Dylan ]
♪ Jingle bells, jingle bells ♪

00:09:52.234 --> 00:09:53.667
[ Laughter ]

00:09:53.667 --> 00:09:56.567
